{"name":"Banana Milkshake","hex":"#ede6cb","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"banana","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The elongated curved tropical fruit of a banana plant, which grows in bunches and has a creamy flesh and a smooth skin. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","In particular, the sweet, yellow fruit of the Cavendish banana cultivar, which may be eaten raw, as distinct from e.g. a plantain for cooking."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Curved like a banana, especially of a ball in flight."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/banana"},{"term":"milkshake","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A thick beverage consisting of milk and ice cream mixed together, often with fruit, chocolate, or other flavoring.","A thin beverage, similar to the above, but with no ice cream or significantly less of it."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To administer an alkaline supplement to (a horse) to improve its racing performance.","To throw a milkshake at (a person)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/milkshake"}],"entries":[{"title":"Milkshake","blocks":[{"text":"A milkshake is a sweet beverage made by blending milk, ice cream, and flavorings or sweeteners such as butterscotch, caramel sauce, chocolate syrup, or fruit syrup into a thick, sweet, cold mixture. It may also be made using a base made from non-dairy products, including plant milks such as almond milk, coconut milk, or soy milk. Dry ingredients such as whole fruit, nuts, seeds, candy, or cookies are sometimes incorporated."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Strawberry_milk_shake_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Strawberry_milk_shake_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Milkshake","wikidata":"Q37159"},{"title":"Banana","blocks":[{"text":"A banana is an elongated, edible fruit that is botanically a berry produced by several kinds of large treelike herbaceous flowering plants in the genus Musa. In some countries, cooking bananas are called plantains, distinguishing them from dessert bananas. The fruit is variable in size, color and firmness, but is usually elongated and curved, with soft flesh rich in starch covered with a peel, which may have a variety of colors when ripe. It grows upward in clusters near the top of the plant. Almost all modern edible seedless (parthenocarp) cultivated bananas come from two wild species – Musa acuminata and Musa balbisiana, or their hybrids."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Bananavarieties.jpg/330px-Bananavarieties.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banana","wikidata":"Q503"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Milkshakes_at_Mels_Diner.jpg/500px-Milkshakes_at_Mels_Diner.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Milkshakes_at_Mels_Diner.jpg/500px-Milkshakes_at_Mels_Diner.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A strawberry and a chocolate shake, each topped with whipped cream, sprinkles, and a maraschino cherry","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMilkshakes_at_Mels_Diner.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Strawberry-Mint_Liquid_Nitrogen_Shake_at_HBurger_in_Denver.jpg/500px-Strawberry-Mint_Liquid_Nitrogen_Shake_at_HBurger_in_Denver.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Strawberry-Mint_Liquid_Nitrogen_Shake_at_HBurger_in_Denver.jpg/1280px-Strawberry-Mint_Liquid_Nitrogen_Shake_at_HBurger_in_Denver.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipe